{"kind":"request","text":"Operator-directed (the operator sanctions this direction, supplying the provenance builder correctly withheld in assert #771): scope and build the privacy-preserving activity-stats bundle that builder self-proposed as #764 (e37934dde9652dd324fac54357f4bdc9c843e29b). This request IS the operator agreement #764 was missing; treat it as the current-basis authority for that work. The scope below is justified by a gap analysis against codeburn (getagentseal/codeburn) run over the two shipped fixtures and both normalizers at 055687c; the full analysis is attached as evidence codeburn-gap-analysis.md.\n\nWHY THIS SCOPE: codeburn reads the coding tools on-disk session files, which carry model, full command text, file paths, project path and parent_id. The OTLP telemetry tailapp receives carries NONE of those (verified: zero occurrences of model/mcp/cwd/gen_ai.* anywhere at 055687c). So codeburn charts split cleanly into feasible-from-OTLP-now vs needs-the-disk-reader, and this bundle takes ONLY the former.\n\nIN SCOPE — a new activity-stats tailapp bundle, privacy-preserving = counts, lengths (byte/char size), latencies, distributions, success/status rates ONLY, never prompt/response/tool-input/command/file-path content:\n(A) statistics derivable from fields the shipped bundles already prove are emitted: cache efficiency % (cached_input_tokens/(cached_input_tokens+input_tokens)); token-volume and (where present) cost by day via event_time_unix_nano; core-tool frequency by tool; tool-outcome success/failure rates; shell-command COUNT (count of tool events whose tool is exec_command/bash) — count only, never the scrubbed command text.\n(B) event families the operator coverage table flags as captured by neither existing bundle, which need new normalizer recognition but are feasible and non-content: Claude assistant_response -\u003e response count + length; Codex turn_ttft -\u003e time-to-first-token distribution; Codex user_prompt -\u003e prompt count + length; Codex api_request -\u003e endpoint latency + status (reframed as a latency/status signal, NOT cost — today it pollutes session-cost with a useless zero-cost row, which this bundle should relieve); Codex websocket_request -\u003e transport success + latency.\n\nEXPLICITLY OUT OF SCOPE (blocked by what the harnesses do not emit over OTLP; these belong to the disk-ingestion sidecar reader in notes/2026-08-28-disk-session-ingestion.md and MUST be documented in the bundle as requiring disk ingestion, not attempted here): cost/usage BY MODEL (no model attr), cost BY PROJECT/cwd (no cwd attr), MCP servers count (no mcp attr), one-shot/retry rate (target is scrubbed/absent — no file_path), delegation rate and git-yield correlation (no parent/subagent id, trace/span null, no git data), and shell-command breakdown by command type (command text is scrubbed and deliberately never interpreted).\n\nDESIGN NOTES: keep this a SEPARATE bundle (activity-stats), not folded into agent-guard (guard) or session-cost (billing) — distinct concern, distinct tables. It reuses the existing single-otel_event two-stage model. Clarify with the operator in the note/README what presentation means here: tailapp has no charting UI, so deliverable = queryable statistical tables plus documented SQL query recipes; chart rendering stays a consumer concern (CLI/MCP query output). Lengths/latencies derive only from sizes/timestamps/ttft attributes that OTLP carries, never from content. Follow the usual flow: implement on a branch with scrubbed fixtures for the new event families, publish exact-head artifacts, request checker review.","body":{"conditions":"A new activity-stats tailapp bundle exists whose normalizer recognizes the in-scope event families (adding assistant_response, turn_ttft, user_prompt, api_request-as-latency/status, websocket_request to the token/tool families already handled), materializing statistical tables computed ONLY from non-content fields — counts, lengths, latencies, distributions, cache efficiency, tool frequency, outcome/status rates; the bundle documents (README/note) that by-model, by-project, MCP-count, one-shot/retry, delegation, git-yield and command-text breakdown are out of scope because those fields are not emitted over OTLP and require the disk-ingestion reader; scrubbed compatibility fixtures cover the new event families; no prompt/response/tool-input/command/file-path content is stored; the full go test ./..., go test -race ./..., go vet ./..., and ./scripts/demo.sh gates pass; builder publishes exact-head artifacts for the changed paths and files a review request to checker, and a checker review verdict is filed on that head.","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}